@startuml 04_Request_Group_Key

title 04. Fetch Conversation Data - After Generating New Identity Key

actor "User\n(Requester)" as User
participant "Requester\nClient" as Client
participant "Crypto Layer" as Crypto
participant "Device Storage" as Storage
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Helper\nClient" as Helper
participant "Helper\nCrypto" as HelperCrypto

User -> Client: Fetch conversation
activate Client

Client -> Server: GET /conversations/{conv_id}
activate Server
Server --> Client: Conversation data\n{member_key: NULL, ...}
deactivate Server

Client -> Client: Check member_key == NULL

Client --> User: "Group key required"
deactivate Client

User -> Client: Request group key
activate Client

Client -> Crypto: Generate temp key pair
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  Generate ephemeral key pair
  (X25519 or similar)
  - publicKey: shareable
  - privateKey: kept secret
end note

Crypto -> Crypto: tempKeyPair = generateKeyPair()
Crypto --> Client: {publicKey, privateKey}
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Storage: Store {privateKey, group_key_version}
activate Storage
note right of Storage
  Associate privateKey with
  specific group_key_version
  for later decryption
end note
Storage --> Client: Stored
deactivate Storage

Client -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/request-group-key\n{publicKey, group_key_version}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Verify requester is member

Server -> Server: Find online helper\n(prefer admin)

Server -> WS: Notify helper\n{requester_id, publicKey, group_key_version}
activate WS
WS -> Helper: Group key request notification
deactivate WS

Server --> Client: "Request sent, waiting for helper"
deactivate Server

activate Helper

Helper -> Helper: Check if has group_key_version

alt Has group key version

    Helper -> HelperCrypto: Decrypt own member_key
    activate HelperCrypto
    note right of HelperCrypto
      member_key decryption:
      group_key = Decrypt(
        member_key,
        helper_identity_secret
      )
    end note
    HelperCrypto --> Helper: group_key (plaintext)
    deactivate HelperCrypto
    
    Helper -> HelperCrypto: Encrypt for requester
    activate HelperCrypto
    note right of HelperCrypto
      Asymmetric encryption:
      encrypted_group_key = Encrypt_Asymmetric(
        group_key,
        requester_publicKey
      )
      
      Uses ECIES/NaCl Box
      Server CANNOT decrypt
    end note
    HelperCrypto -> HelperCrypto: Sign encrypted payload
    HelperCrypto --> Helper: {encrypted_group_key, signature}
    deactivate HelperCrypto
    
    Helper -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/provide-group-key\n{requester_id, encrypted_group_key, signature}
    activate Server
    
    Server -> Server: Verify:\n- Helper is member\n- Signature valid
    
    Server -> WS: Forward to requester
    activate WS
    WS -> Client: {encrypted_group_key}
    deactivate WS
    
    Server --> Helper: "Sent successfully"
    deactivate Server

else Does not have group key version
    Helper --> User: "Cannot help - don't have this version"
    note right of Helper
      If no helper has the version,
      user remains locked out until
      someone with that version comes online
    end note
end

deactivate Helper

Client -> Storage: Retrieve privateKey
activate Storage
Storage --> Client: privateKey
deactivate Storage

Client -> Crypto: Decrypt group key
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  Asymmetric decryption:
  group_key = Decrypt_Asymmetric(
    encrypted_group_key,
    privateKey
  )
  
  Only requester can decrypt
end note
Crypto --> Client: group_key (plaintext)
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Crypto: Encrypt member_key
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  member_key = Encrypt(
    group_key,
    identity_secret
  )
end note
Crypto --> Client: member_key
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/update-member-key\n{member_key}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Integrity checks:\n- member_key was NULL?\n- Requester is member?

Server -> Server: UPDATE member_key\n(only if was NULL)

Server --> Client: "Member key updated"
deactivate Server

Client -> Storage: Discard privateKey\n(single-use)
activate Storage
Storage --> Client: Deleted
deactivate Storage

Client --> User: "Access restored"
deactivate Client

note over User, HelperCrypto
  Security properties:
  ✅ Server never sees group_key plaintext
  ✅ Asymmetric encryption prevents server decryption
  ✅ Temporary key pair discarded after use
  ✅ Only requester can decrypt with privateKey
  ⚠️ User locked out if no helper online
end note

@enduml
